t prior to  the december launch little other details  are known about this upcoming event but  the secrets are apparently uncovered by  completing challenges across both  vanguard and warzone each game will have  its own set of tasks and rewards for  completing them one of which activision  describes as acquiring and protecting  pacific artifacts while fighting to  survive in verdansk it's possible  secrets of the pacific will work  similarly to past events like the  haunting and the numbers event which  offered weapons and cosmetic items for  completing set objectives however no  rewards have been mentioned by  activision just yet one final event is  scheduled for players to save farewell  to warzone's original location though  from november 30th until the preseason's  end war zone will feature the last hours  of verdansk which is vaguely described  as watching to see what happens to  berdansk before war zone goes dark to  prepare for caldera  activision also says to expect a  spectacular and fitting into your time  in verdansk as we say farewell to  castobian city forever  the new caldera map is set to launch on  december 8th for vanguard owners and on  the 9th for everyone else  battlefield 2042 has already attracted  millions of players after its full  release on november 19th but the  multiplayer only battlefield title has  fans expressing disappointment with a  buggy launch and lack of legacy features  but today dice has restated its  commitment to the game promising in a  blog post that it will be supporting and  evolving it for years to come the post  gives a road map on planned updates and  changes coming to battlefield 2042  starting with update number two which is  due to release on thursday november 25th  this update will be followed by an even  larger update number three in early  december with dice saying that a further  update after this will hopefully be out  before the holidays as well further down  the track the studio will start  revealing details about the game's first  season in 2022 the developer also  restated its commitment to including  various legacy features that aren't  present in the current version of the  game though it doesn't currently have a  timeline for these features into the  match scoreboard server browser and  features like voice chat are big topics  for us to cover all at once and we have  plenty we want to say around them the  post reads we'll come back to you when  we have things that we can show you  including details about our long term  vision for certain features and  functions update number two will also  include some changes to the hovercraft a  vehicle that early players found had the  ability to travel vertically of  buildings since the game went live we  saw the hovercraft become a fan favorite  given its high durability and  effectiveness in combat the post reads  we designed this vehicle to behave as an  alternative to the latview 4 but not as  an upgrade in thursday's update number 2  we have balanced the health of this  vehicle to bring it more in line with  its design and made sure that its  weaponry is appropriately effective even  more details for update number two are  said to be on the way and there have  been some details on update number three  mentioned already if you want the full  rundown of every note we have so far be  sure to check out our full write-up on  gamespot.com  kojima has posted a cryptic teaser for  what looks like a new project and people  believe norman reedus may be involved  again kojima posted the teaser photo  with the caption recently i've been  revising the plan and script and  experimenting with everything else and  someone in the foreground looks like it  could possibly be norman reedus but  nothing is confirmed of course what are  you hoping will be kojima's next big  reveal let me know in the comments and  hopefully your prediction comes true and  we'll see something at the game awards  leave a like subscribe and make sure you  all have